{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/901749-olympians-series-by-george-o-connor","id":901749,"title":"\"Olympians\" series by George O'Connor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T22:17:16-07:00","id":901749,"title":"\"Olympians\" series by George O'Connor","content":"I came across this young people's series at work and have quite enjoyed it. Its a pretty basic retelling of the myths surrounding each Greek God, but what I have found particularly clever are little bits of human motivation and intrigue woven into the myths, my favourite being Persephone lying about eating the pomegranate seed after getting some &quot;wink-wink&quot; advise from Hermes (the rascal lol) on the rules of the Underworld. In this telling she has come to realize that Hades is regal and kind in his own lonely way and she is not so eager to return to her mother so she tells a little white lie to get her 6 months with him.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.olympiansrule.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.olympiansrule.com</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T23:04:39-07:00","id":901786,"title":"","content":"I like the character designs. I think I correctly identified everyone in the big &quot;family photo&quot;. I'm only unsure on the woman faded in the back - I'm assuming that's either meant to be Rhea or Gaea, and the three women on the far right (I'd guess Graces, but two of their dresses matching while a third is different is throwing me).","signature":"<